/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-23-  // Int / float true division. OPAQUE for kprove (no-evaluators); concrete for krun.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-24-  syntax Float ::= intFloatDiv(Int, Float) [function, total, symbol(intFloatDiv), no-evaluators]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-25-  rule intFloatDiv(I:Int, F:Float) => Int2Float(I, 53, 11) /Float F [concrete]
